==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[peritonaeum]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|περί|περί-|around|tr=peri|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|τόνος||stretch|tr=tonos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|-αιος||suffix to form an adjective|tr=-aios|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|peritonea}}

# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} In [[mammal]]s, the [[serous membrane]] lining the cavity of the abdomen and that is folded over the [[viscera]].
# {{context|zoology|lang=en}} In [[animal]]s, the membrane lining the [[coelom]] cavity.

====Derived terms====
* [[peritoneal]]
* [[peritoneally]]
* [[peritonitis]]

